From: Balena RK3588 integration
Subject: [PATCH] nvme: scan: enumerate PCI before probing NVMe devices

This vendor tree's common/board_r.c guards its pci_init() call with
"#ifndef CONFIG_DM_PCI", so with CONFIG_DM_PCI the PCIe controllers are
never enumerated at boot and no PCI child devices (including NVMe
controllers) are ever bound.  The "nvme scan" loop over UCLASS_NVME then
iterates an empty uclass and returns silently, which makes every later
"nvme dev N" fail with "** Bad device nvme N **".

Call pci_init() at the start of nvme_scan_namespace(): the DM version
probes every UCLASS_PCI controller and, as a side effect of probing,
enumerates the buses and binds the NVMe child devices the loop below is
meant to probe.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/drivers/nvme/nvme.c	2026-08-27 14:06:58.339750973 +0800
+++ b/drivers/nvme/nvme.c	2026-08-27 14:06:58.352855325 +0800
@@ -705,6 +705,14 @@
 	struct udevice *dev;
 	int ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * This tree only enumerates PCI at boot for non-DM builds (see the
+	 * CONFIG_DM_PCI guard around pci_init() in common/board_r.c), so
+	 * probe the PCIe controllers here first; bus enumeration binds the
+	 * NVMe child devices that the loop below probes.
+	 */
+	pci_init();
+
 	ret = uclass_get(UCLASS_NVME, &uc);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
